{title: 112 - Let Us With a Gladsome Mind}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #112 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 112}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Let [Gm]us [F]with [Bb]a[Eb]glad[Cm]some [Bb]mind
[Bb]Praise the [F]Lord, [Bb]for [F]He [C7]is [F]kind:
[F]For [C]His [F]mer[F7]cies [Bb]shall en[F]dure,
[Bb]Ev[F]er [F7]faith[Bb]ful, [C7]ev[F7]er [Bb]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb][Gm]He, [F]with [Bb][Eb]all [Cm]commanding [Bb]might,
[Bb]Filled [F]the [Bb]new [F]made [C7]world [F]with light:
[F][C]For [F]His [F7]mercies [Bb]shall [F]endure,
[Bb][F]Ever [F7][Bb]faithful, [C7][F7]ever [Bb]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb][Gm]All [F]things [Bb]living [Eb]He [Cm]does [Bb]feed;
[Bb]His [F]full [Bb]hand [F]supplies [C7]their [F]need:
[F][C]For [F]His [F7]mercies [Bb]shall [F]endure,
[Bb][F]Ever [F7][Bb]faithful, [C7][F7]ever [Bb]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb][Gm]Let [F]us [Bb]then [Eb]with [Cm]gladsome [Bb]mind
[Bb]Praise [F]the [Bb]Lord, [F]for [C7]He [F]is kind:
[F][C]For [F]His [F7]mercies [Bb]shall [F]endure,
[Bb][F]Ever [F7][Bb]faithful, [C7][F7]ever [Bb]sure.
{end_of_verse}
